1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,130
What if your phone showed tomorrow's photos?

2
00:00:03,170 --> 00:00:05,917
You open the gallery and there's a picture

3
00:00:05,957 --> 00:00:07,376
you haven't taken yet:

4
00:00:07,416 --> 00:00:08,770
you, covered in cake,

5
00:00:08,810 --> 00:00:11,026
standing in a very confused crowd.

6
00:00:11,750 --> 00:00:13,237
So you dodge the cake.

7
00:00:13,277 --> 00:00:16,221
Next morning, you spot the exact same room,

8
00:00:16,261 --> 00:00:18,164
but now it's perfectly calm.

9
00:00:18,204 --> 00:00:19,413
The photo changed.

10
00:00:19,453 --> 00:00:23,161
Apparently, tomorrow only exists until you look at it.

11
00:00:23,650 --> 00:00:25,165
Photos become a habit.

12
00:00:25,205 --> 00:00:26,226
A winning goal.

13
00:00:26,266 --> 00:00:27,074
A new puppy.

14
00:00:27,114 --> 00:00:29,125
A rainy day with no umbrella.

15
00:00:29,165 --> 00:00:30,680
You carry an umbrella.

16
00:00:30,720 --> 00:00:31,741
You win a goal.

17
00:00:31,781 --> 00:00:33,862
Your friends call you psychic,

18
00:00:33,902 --> 00:00:35,983
and you politely refuse a hat.

19
00:00:37,450 --> 00:00:39,986
Then one photo makes your stomach drop.

20
00:00:40,026 --> 00:00:42,034
It's your grandfather's garden,

21
00:00:42,074 --> 00:00:44,677
empty, with one chair left in the grass.

22
00:00:44,717 --> 00:00:46,791
You stare at it for a long while

23
00:00:46,831 --> 00:00:49,037
before you realise: you have time.

24
00:00:50,450 --> 00:00:51,985
You head to the garden.

25
00:00:52,025 --> 00:00:54,656
He is there, humming over the tomatoes,

26
00:00:54,696 --> 00:00:56,231
and you stay for hours.

27
00:00:56,271 --> 00:00:58,354
The new photo shows two chairs,

28
00:00:58,394 --> 00:01:00,614
two cups, and a very smug tomato.

29
00:01:00,654 --> 00:01:02,463
Some futures can be edited.

30
00:01:04,250 --> 00:01:07,018
Scientists would say a phone cannot see the

31
00:01:07,058 --> 00:01:10,087
future, because the future hasn't happened yet.

32
00:01:10,128 --> 00:01:11,851
In this thought experiment,

33
00:01:11,891 --> 00:01:14,332
the gallery is less a crystal ball and

34
00:01:14,372 --> 00:01:15,965
more a gentle suggestion.

35
00:01:16,550 --> 00:01:17,728
Here is the twist.

36
00:01:17,768 --> 00:01:19,283
One last photo appears:

37
00:01:19,323 --> 00:01:21,448
you, today, standing right here,

38
00:01:21,488 --> 00:01:24,695
holding your phone, staring at that exact photo.

39
00:01:24,735 --> 00:01:28,009
You look up, and the camera in the corner blinks.

40
00:01:28,850 --> 00:01:30,419
So you pocket the phone,

41
00:01:30,459 --> 00:01:31,693
grin at the camera,

42
00:01:31,733 --> 00:01:33,637
and strike a ridiculous pose.

43
00:01:33,677 --> 00:01:35,849
Tomorrow's photo updates at once:

44
00:01:35,889 --> 00:01:38,062
you laughing, sunrise behind you,

45
00:01:38,102 --> 00:01:40,274
with absolutely no cake in sight.
